! 3C-SiC: the Berry-phase polarization on an **ultrasoft** dataset, and the case
! where the augmentation charge actually has to be right.
!
! Silicon and AlAs both give a soft dataset an easy time here. Silicon is
! centrosymmetric, so its electronic phase is zero whatever `q_ij(b)` does; AlAs
! has a nonzero one but is norm-conserving, where the augmentation term is
! identically absent. Zincblende SiC is both at once -- `-43m`, so nothing forces
! the phase to zero, and two ultrasoft datasets, so the overlap between
! neighbouring k-points carries `q_ij(b)` and is wrong without it.
!
! Both pseudopotentials were already committed for other cases; this is the pair
! `NEXT-SESSION.md` identified as the one that unblocks the ultrasoft
! piezoelectric tensor, used here for the polarization it is built on.
!
! `nosym`/`noinv` and the tight `conv_thr` for `alas-berry.in`'s reasons.
 &control
    calculation = 'nscf'
    lberry = .true.
    gdir = 3
    nppstr = 6
    prefix = 'sic'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 8.24, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 24.0, ecutrho = 192.0,
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si 28.086 Si.pz-n-rrkjus_psl.0.1.UPF
 C  12.011 C.pz-rrkjus.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 C  0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 2 2 6 0 0 0
